# GoClaw — Architecture

## Identity
Go CLI agent, Claude Code–style. Module: `github.com/okuzpe/goclaw`. Go 1.26. Default provider: local Ollama (`qwen2.5-coder:14b`).

## Workspace scope
Sibling folders such as `claw-code/` in the parent directory are **reference only**; they are not part of this module or goclaw’s roadmap. Implement and commit only under `goclaw/`.

## Entry point layout (`cmd/goclaw/`)

| File | Responsibility |
|------|---------------|
| `main.go` | slog default, `cli.NewRootCmd` with `app.RunChat(cmd, Version, args, fullscreenChat{})` |
| `tui.go` | `FullscreenChatRunner` implementation (Bubble Tea); links `internal/ui/chat` so `internal/app` tests do not |
| `version.go` | `Version` var for `-ldflags -X` |

> **Rule:** No `*_test.go` under `cmd/goclaw` — tests that need the full REPL graph live in `internal/cli`, `internal/slashcmd`, `internal/app` (without importing `ui/chat`). Keeps `go test ./internal/app` reliable on Windows (Bubble Tea stack can block non-TTY test binaries if linked from `app`).

All REPL wiring, banner, and slash handlers live under `internal/app`, `internal/cli`, `internal/slashcmd`.

## Package map

| Package | Single responsibility |
|---------|----------------------|
| `cmd/goclaw/` | Thin `main` + TUI wiring + `Version` |
| `internal/cli/` | Cobra tree (`NewRootCmd`); inject `RunChat` / `RunListSessions` for testability without linking TUI |
| `internal/app/` | `RunChat`, `RunListSessions`, banner; default Bubble Tea TUI on TTY; readline with `--readline` / `GOCLAW_USE_TUI=0` |
| `internal/slashcmd/` | REPL `/` slash command handlers + `$EDITOR` prompt |
| `internal/llm/` | `Client` interface + Anthropic (SSE) + Ollama (NDJSON) + OpenAI-compat (SSE `/v1/chat/completions`) + HTTP retry |
| `internal/session/` | In-memory history, JSONL serialization, store |
| `internal/orchestrator/` | Main loop: user → LLM → tools → repeat (32 iter / 64 tool calls) |
| `internal/tools/` | `Tool` interface + `Registry` + ten built-in tools + limits |
| `internal/permissions/` | `Policy.Evaluate(toolName)` + `ApplyConfigModes` for `tool_permissions` |
| `internal/config/` | `Config`, `Default()`, hierarchical load (user → project → local) |
| `internal/hooks/` | Go handler registry + external subprocess/HTTP hooks + project hooks file |
| `internal/agents/` | Seven built-in profiles + `All()` lookup; custom agents from `~/.goclaw/agents` and `.goclaw/agents` |
| `internal/memory/` | Filesystem store under `~/.goclaw/memory/`, MEMORY.md index |
| `internal/mcp/` | Stdio JSON-RPC MCP client: process lifecycle, tool discovery, `mcp__id__name` naming |
| `internal/planfile/` | Workspace `.goclaw/plan.md` path, template, size limits, handoff message |
| `internal/todos/` | Session-scoped task list store (`todo_write` tool backend) |
| `internal/ide/` | Optional localhost POST notifier (`GOCLAW_IDE_NOTIFY_URL`) after each tool |
| `internal/ui/chat/` | BubbleTea TUI model (viewport + text input + streaming + compact approval strip above input) |
| `testutil/mockserver/` | HTTP mock for Anthropic tests without API tokens |

## Structure rules
- Terminal / TUI output: follow `.cursor/rules/terminal-rendering.mdc` (Charm stack + `ui_appearance`; use `config.GlamourTermRendererOptions` from `app` instead of importing `ui/chat`).
- One package = one responsibility. Do not merge packages.
- No circular imports between `internal/*` packages.
- `cmd/` imports `internal/` only, never the reverse.
- Define interfaces in the package that consumes them, not the implementor.
- `internal/ui/chat/` uses BubbleTea Elm pattern: **all state mutations in `Update()`**; async work via `tea.Cmd`, never raw goroutines inside the model.

## Glossary
- **tool** — Go type implementing `internal/tools.Tool`
- **agent** / **profile** — `Profile` with model override, tool allowlist, read-only flag, system prompt
- **skill** — reusable Markdown prompt template (`.claude/skills/`)
- **command** — REPL **slash command** (`/help`, `/compact`, `/memory`); not a Cobra subcommand
- **CLI subcommand** — Cobra entry (e.g. `goclaw sessions list`)
- **hook** — handler for a `hooks.EventType` (Go `On(...)` or external subprocess/HTTP)
- **session** — conversation history (RAM + JSONL on disk at `~/.goclaw/sessions/`)
- **memory** — durable facts under `~/.goclaw/memory/`

## Implemented status (2026-04)
- **Done:** core loop, Ollama + Anthropic clients + retry, session JSONL store, default BubbleTea TUI on TTY (readline opt-in), Cobra CLI, all 10 tools (read_file/glob/grep/bash/write_file/edit_file/patch/web_fetch/web_search/todo_write), permissions, memory, compaction, hooks (Go + external + project file), MCP stdio client (multi-server), IDE notifier, planfile + `/apply-plan`, all slash commands, hub-and-spoke coordinator (`spawn_agent` / `stop_task`, profile `coordinator`; see monorepo `docs/goclaw/coordinator.md`).
- **Post-MVP v2+:** Team/Swarm peer-agent topology (distinct from in-process coordinator); see `docs/reference/coordinator-mode.md` at monorepo root.
- **Post-MVP v3+:** Plugins, full IDE bridge, remote MCP transports, OAuth.
